<title>NORWAY: Norway in talks with Poland over gas sales.</title>
<headline>Norway in talks with Poland over gas sales.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Gas Negotiating Committee has held a preliminary meeting with Polish Oil and Gas Company (POGC) on the possible sale of Norwegian gas to Poland, Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Polish gas demand is forecast to rise to about 25 billion cubic metres per year by 2010 from around 10 to 11 billion now, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Poland's annual production is about 3.6 billion cubic metres, with Russia supplying the remainder of its needs.</p>
<p>POGC recently agreed to buy a further 13 billion cubic metres per year from Russia's Gazprom, but sales from Norway would diversify Poland's sources of supply, Statoil said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
